@payments = http://localhost:4003

### Own balance (workflow step 5)
# {{player_token}} is the launch session token (02); it is valid for payments.
# Payments consumes engagement.spin.completed and credits coins with the key spin:<spin_id>.
# The read is eventually consistent for a moment after the spin; the ledger itself is exact.
GET {{payments}}/v1/me/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{player_token}}

# Response (captured from scripts/demo.sh, after a 200-coin spin):
# HTTP/1.1 200 OK
# {"wallet_id":"01a2012d-4b5f-7089-bb44-30ea714130c2","available":200,"held":0,"currency":"COIN"}

### Operator reads one player's balance (own tenant only, production wallet)
# The operator token needs the payments audience (login with "audience": "payments", see 01).
GET {{payments}}/v1/players/{{player_id}}/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{operator_payments_token}}

# Response (captured from scripts/demo.sh on 2026-11-22, run on dd9d464; after a 500-coin spin and one 50-coin redemption):
# HTTP/1.1 200 OK
# {"wallet_id":"01a20399-e459-741c-bc03-7118046b196e","available":450,"held":0,"currency":"COIN"}

### There is no route that credits coins. This must not exist.
POST {{payments}}/v1/credits
Authorization: Bearer {{operator_payments_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "player_id": "{{player_id}}", "amount": 1000 }

# Response (shape from the contract, not captured):
# HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found
